      "heading": "Introduction to Machine Learning",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "Machine learning teaches computers to learn from data.",
          "timestamp": "00:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "It replaces explicit rules with data-driven learning.",
          "timestamp": "00:00"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Supervised Learning",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "System trained on labeled data.",
          "timestamp": "00:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Example: email marked as spam or not spam.",
          "timestamp": "00:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Model learns patterns to predict unseen cases.",
          "timestamp": "00:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Common algorithms: decision trees, SVMs, neural networks.",
          "timestamp": "00:00"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Unsupervised Learning",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "System finds patterns without labels.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Example: clustering customers by purchasing behavior.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "K-means is a classic algorithm.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Reinforcement Learning",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "Agent interacts with an environment.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Learns from feedback or rewards.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Example: AI playing video games or controlling a robot.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Challenges in Machine Learning",
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": "Overfitting: model memorizes training data, performs poorly on new data.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bias: occurs when training data is unbalanced.",
          "timestamp": "01:00"
        }
      ]
    },
